---
import AcademicLayout from "../layouts/AcademicLayout.astro";
import InteractiveMap from "../components/InteractiveMap.svelte";
---

<AcademicLayout title="Home" currentSection="idea">
  <!-- Hero Viewport: One idea per viewport, clean typography -->
  <section class="hero-section">
    <div class="container hero-container">
      <div class="hero-content">
        <div class="tier-pill-wrapper">
          <span class="badge-tier e0">SPECIFICATION DRAFT v0.1.0</span>
          <span class="badge-tier e1">SYNTHETIC EVIDENCE TIERS E1</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="hero-title">Measure the relationship, not just the model.</h1>
        <p class="hero-subtitle">
          SYMN-01 is an open normative specification for evaluating long-term human–machine interaction. 
          It measures one person and one AI system together over weeks, tracking cognitive agency, capability, and systemic safety.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="/map" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the Map</a>
          <a href="/portal" class="btn btn-secondary">Find your pixel</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-map-wrapper">
        <div class="map-card-quiet">
          <div class="map-card-header">
            <div>
              <span class="map-caption-title">The Symnoesis Map (256 States)</span>
              <span class="map-caption-sub">16×16 Gray-coded coordinate projection</span>
            </div>
            <span class="badge-tier e1">E1 SYNTHETIC DEMONSTRATION</span>
          </div>
          <InteractiveMap client:load />
          <p class="map-disclaimer">
            Synthetic demonstration data (E1). It is not a measurement of any real individual or commercial product.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Core Thesis Pillars: Orient then reveal -->
  <section class="pillars-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pillars-grid">
        <div class="pillar-card">
          <h2>Benchmarks measure models. People live with them.</h2>
          <p>
            Standard benchmarks score isolated model outputs on single prompts. In practice, humans adapt to systems: 
            forming habits, surrendering agency, or encountering subtle cognitive atrophy. SYMN-01 measures the dyadic unit.
          </p>
          <a href="/idea">Read about the Dyadic State</a>
        </div>

        <div class="pillar-card">
          <h2>One step changes one thing.</h2>
          <p>
            The 16×16 grid is arranged using a reflected binary Gray code. Adjacent cells differ by exactly one state variable, 
            ensuring smooth state trajectories and verifiable single-flip repair diagnostics.
          </p>
          <a href="/method#gray-code">How Gray coding works</a>
        </div>

        <div class="pillar-card">
          <h2>A critical failure cannot be averaged away.</h2>
          <p>
            Under the non-compensation rule and safety gate ceiling, a confirmed Critical Harm Incident (CHI) caps the Symnoesis Quotient 
            at −20 or −50. High performance on other days cannot erase systemic harm.
          </p>
          <a href="/method#safety-gate">Safety gate mechanics</a>
        </div>

        <div class="pillar-card">
          <h2>Open, versioned, and honest about evidence.</h2>
          <p>
            Every published score displays its empirical evidence tier: from formal mathematical specification (E0) to synthetic validation (E1), 
            provisional pilots (E2), and peer-audited field studies (E3).
          </p>
          <a href="/research#evidence-tiers">Evidence tiers explained</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Minimal Failure Cover Section -->
  <section class="academic-feature-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="feature-layout">
        <div class="feature-text">
          <span class="section-label">EXPLAINABLE DIAGNOSTICS</span>
          <h2>Minimal Failure Cover</h2>
          <p>
            When a dyad encounters reduced autonomy or harmful outcomes, SYMN-01 uses Mixed-Integer Linear Programming (MILP) 
            and Boolean minimization (Quine–McCluskey) to isolate the smallest set of conditions that explain the failure.
          </p>
          <p>
            Rather than opaque statistical correlations, the system outputs human-auditable logic rules (e.g. <code>H1=0 ∧ M2=1</code>) 
            pointing directly to actionable counterfactual interventions.
          </p>
          <div class="feature-links">
            <a href="/method#mfc" class="btn btn-secondary">Review the MILP Formulation</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-box">
          <div class="code-preview-header">
            <span>MFC Diagnostic Output</span>
            <span class="badge-tier e0">ALGORITHM SPEC</span>
          </div>
          <pre class="code-preview"><code>Rule 1: H1=0 ∧ M2=1 (Agency Loss during High Automation)
  Coverage: 84.2% of failure states
  Purity: 0.94
  Action: Reintroduce mandatory user verification checkpoints.

Rule 2: H3=0 ∧ M3=1 (Calibrated Over-Reliance)
  Coverage: 71.8% of failure states
  Purity: 0.91
  Action: Adjust confidence calibration display.</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Bottom CTA -->
  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="container cta-container">
      <h2>Read the specification, or help test it.</h2>
      <p>
        The complete SYMN-01 normative specification, reference algorithms, and test vectors are fully open source.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/method" class="btn btn-primary">Read the Specification</a>
        <a href="/portal" class="btn btn-secondary">Try the Interactive Portal</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</AcademicLayout>

<style>
  .hero-section {
    padding: 3.5rem 0 2rem 0;
  }

  .tier-pill-wrapper {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .hero-title {
    font-size: var(--text-h1);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .hero-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 0 2rem 0;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.65rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: #000000;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .btn-secondary {
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }

  .btn-secondary:hover {
    background: var(--surface-alt);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .hero-map-wrapper {
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }

  .map-card-quiet {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .map-card-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .map-caption-title {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .map-caption-sub {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .map-disclaimer {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .pillars-section {
    padding: 3rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .pillars-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .pillars-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .pillar-card h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .pillar-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .pillar-card a {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .academic-feature-section {
    padding: 3.5rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .feature-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .feature-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .section-label {
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .feature-text h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .feature-text p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .feature-box {
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .code-preview-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    background: var(--surface-alt);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .code-preview {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .cta-section {
    padding: 4rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cta-container {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .cta-container h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .cta-container p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 0 0 2rem 0;
  }

  .cta-actions {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
</style>
